# TwinTack API Integrations & Third-Party Services Rules

## Custom Grip Workflow (Primary)

**Native production workflow** is handled entirely in WordPress via **twintack-custom-grips**. See `plugins/twintack-custom-grips/WORKFLOW.md` for the canonical status flow.

- **twintack-custom-grips** — Team dashboard, customer My Custom Grips, statuses, mockups, messaging, notifications
- **twintack-grip-manager** — `grip_design` CPT, Gravity Forms intake, purchase-based post creation, WooCommerce order → artwork status bridge

Monday.com and Make.com are **retired** for the grip production workflow. Do not build new features against those integrations.

---

## Artwork Status Codes (Current)

| Slug | Label | Notes |
|------|-------|-------|
| `artwork_pending` | Mockup Required | Initial state after deposit |
| `pending_review` | Customer Review | Team uploaded mockup |
| `customer_requested_changes` | Customer Changes | Customer feedback loop |
| `customer_approved` | Customer Approved | Stays until final purchase |
| `in_production` | In Production | Set on WC order Processing |
| `shipped` | Shipped | Set on WC order Completed / shipped-unpaid |

### Legacy slugs (display / migration only)

- `approved_for_production` → maps to `in_production` (removed as team step v1.2.4)
- `artwork_approved`, `internal_review` → legacy records only

### WooCommerce sync

Grip Manager hooks `woocommerce_order_status_changed` and delegates to:

- `TTCG_Status::sync_in_production_from_wc_order()` on `processing`
- `TTCG_Status::sync_shipped_from_wc_order()` on `completed` / `shipped-unpaid`

---

## Monday.com Integration — DEPRECATED

Legacy endpoint still registered in Grip Manager; **do not use for new work**.

- **Endpoint**: `/wp-json/twintack/v1/grip-design/{id}/monday`
- **Method**: POST
- **Authentication**: API key via `X-API-Key` header or `api_key` parameter
- **Default API Key**: `twintack-monday-2024`
- **Custom API Key**: `TWINTACK_MONDAY_API_KEY` in wp-config.php

See `plugins/twintack-grip-manager/MONDAY-API.md` for legacy reference only.

---

## Make.com Integration — DEPRECATED (Grip Workflow)

Legacy Make.com webhooks in Grip Manager (`grip_customer_feedback_webhook_url` filter) applied to the **old** customer feedback path only. The native Custom Grips customer review handler does not use Make.com.

---

## Klaviyo Integration

### Email Marketing Integration

- Use official Klaviyo API for email marketing
- Implement proper API handling with error catching
- Follow Klaviyo's rate limiting guidelines

---

## Gravity Forms Integration

### Form Processing

- **Dependencies**: Grip Manager requires Gravity Forms
- **Entry IDs**: Always store `_grip_form_entry_id` for tracking
- **Form Types**: Support both `original` and `new` form types
- **Field Mapping**: Maintain consistent field mapping between forms

### Form Data Storage

- Store form data in cart metadata before purchase
- Only create grip design posts after successful payment
- Use `_grip_form_type` to distinguish between form versions

---

## API Security Best Practices

### Authentication

- Always use API keys for external integrations
- Implement nonce verification for AJAX requests
- Use WordPress capability checks for admin functions
- Never expose API keys in frontend code

### Data Validation

- Validate all API inputs thoroughly
- Sanitize data using WordPress functions
- Use appropriate WordPress meta functions for storage
- Implement comprehensive error logging

### Rate Limiting

- Implement basic rate limiting for API endpoints
- Monitor API usage through WordPress debug logs
- Handle API failures gracefully with fallback options

---

## Debugging & Monitoring

### Logging Patterns

- Use descriptive prefixes: `TwinTack Custom Grips:`, `TwinTack Grip Manager:`, etc.
- Log all API interactions for debugging
- Include request/response data in logs
- Use WordPress debug logging functions

### Error Handling

- Provide meaningful error messages for debugging
- Return user-friendly error messages in frontend
- Log errors appropriately for different environments
- Handle third-party API failures gracefully

---

## Integration Testing

### Test Scenarios

- Test native workflow end-to-end (form → deposit → mockup → approve → purchase → ship)
- Verify WooCommerce order status sync to artwork status
- Test customer self-service approve/request-changes on My Custom Grips
- Validate role-based status permissions on team dashboard

### Mock Data

- Create mock endpoints for development testing
- Use consistent test data formats
- Implement proper test data cleanup
- Document test scenarios and expected results
